    "Description": "The kernel-rt packages provide the Real Time Linux Kernel, which enables fine-tuning for systems with extremely high determinism requirements.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: netfilter: nfnetlink_cthelper: fix OOB read in nfnl_cthelper_dump_table() (CVE-2026-43450)\n\n* kernel: Bluetooth: hci_event: fix potential UAF in SSP passkey handlers (CVE-2026-46056)\n\n* kernel: procfs: fix missing RCU protection when reading real_parent in do_task_stat() (CVE-2026-46259)\n\n* kernel: dm cache policy smq: fix missing locks in invalidating cache blocks (CVE-2026-53062)\n\n* kernel: ipv6: exthdrs: refresh nh pointer after ipv6_hop_jumbo() (CVE-2026-63924)\n\n* kernel: ipv6: exthdrs: refresh nh after handling HAO option (CVE-2026-63922)\n\n* kernel: ipv6: validate extension header length before copying to cmsg (CVE-2026-63920)\n\n* kernel: selinux: check connect-related permissions on TCP Fast Open (CVE-2026-72243)\n\n* kernel: ipv4: validate checksum_start before completing checksum (CVE-2026-99999)\n\n* kernel: ZDI-CAN-33367: Linux Kernel skbuff skb_zerocopy Improper Ownership Management Local Privilege Escalation Vulnerability ()\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
